From 6113a830c47fd33231e7a7986d41646538cf3f30 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex <alex.a.ackerman@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Apr 2026 13:24:14 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 025/110] fix(plugins): remove rate-limit-watchdog
 (Max-incompatible) (hq-quhi) (#3550)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The rate-limit-watchdog plugin's preflight requires ANTHROPIC_API_KEY and
exits 1 on every dispatch when the var is unset. Towns running on the
Claude Max subscription have no API key to probe with, so every cycle
generates a P0 'plugin-run failed' bead — flooding the inbox with noise
and obscuring real failures.

This plugin is shell-only and probes the Anthropic API directly with
curl. There is no Max-subscription equivalent of an API rate-limit probe
(Max auth doesn't expose 429 the same way), so the simplest fix is to
delete the plugin from gastown source. API-key-based towns that actually
need it can re-add it locally; nothing else in the codebase references
this plugin.

Co-authored-by: navani <user.email=28374790+A3Ackerman@users.noreply.github.com>
